00:03:52,173 --> 00:03:58,173
Everyone has one more fight in them

2
00:07:44,347 --> 00:07:50,347
Rambo: Last Blood is a action, thriller, drama film directed by Adrian Grünberg.

3
00:11:36,521 --> 00:11:42,521
After fighting his demons for decades, John Rambo now lives in peace on his family ranch in Arizona, but his rest is interrupted when
Gabriela, the granddaughter of his housekeeper María, disappears after crossing the border into Mexico to meet her biological father.

4
00:15:28,695 --> 00:15:34,695
Rambo, who has become a true father figure for Gabriela over the years,
undertakes a desperate and dangerous journey to find her.

5
00:19:20,869 --> 00:19:26,869
John Rambo, played by Sylvester Stallone.

6
00:23:13,043 --> 00:23:19,043
Carmen, played by Paz Vega.

7
00:27:05,217 --> 00:27:11,217
Hugo Martínez, played by Sergio Peris-Mencheta.

8
00:30:57,391 --> 00:31:03,391
María Beltrán, played by Adriana Barraza.

9
00:34:49,565 --> 00:34:55,565
Gabriela, played by Yvette Monreal.

10
00:38:41,739 --> 00:38:47,739
Don Manuel, played by Joaquín Cosío.

11
00:42:33,913 --> 00:42:39,913
Rambo: Last Blood is a 2019 American vigilante action film starring
Sylvester Stallone as Vietnam War veteran John Rambo.

12
00:46:26,086 --> 00:46:32,086
Directed by Adrian Grünberg, the film serves as a sequel to Rambo
(2008), and the fifth installment in the Rambo film series.

13
00:50:18,260 --> 00:50:24,260
The story sees Rambo traveling to Mexico to save his adopted niece, who has
been kidnapped by a Mexican cartel and forced into prostitution.

14
00:54:10,434 --> 00:54:16,434
Paz Vega, Sergio Peris-Mencheta, Adriana Barraza, Yvette Monreal, Genie Kim aka
Yenah Han, Joaquín Cosío, and Óscar Jaenada star in supporting roles.

15
00:58:02,608 --> 00:58:08,608
Plans for a fifth film were announced on and off again since 2008,
with different iterations developed and canceled.

16
01:01:54,782 --> 01:02:00,782
The film was finally announced in May 2018, with Grünberg attached to direct.

17
01:05:46,956 --> 01:05:52,956
Principal photography began in October 2018 in Bulgaria and Spain and ended
in December 2018, with additional photography in May 2019.

18
01:09:39,130 --> 01:09:45,130
Brian Tyler returned to score the film.

19
01:13:31,304 --> 01:13:37,304
Rambo: Last Blood was theatrically released on September 20, 2019, to negative reviews from critics, who criticized its script, graphic violence
and perceived racist and xenophobic attitudes towards Mexico, though the action sequences and Stallone's performance were praised.

20
01:17:23,478 --> 01:17:29,478
The film grossed $91.5 million worldwide against a production budget of $50
million and print and advertisement costs of $30 million.

21
01:21:15,652 --> 01:21:21,652
The film explores themes of post-traumatic stress disorder (ptsd),
arizona, human trafficking, affectation, sequel.

22
01:25:07,826 --> 01:25:13,826
The tone is emotional and intense.
